      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Delaying the update preserves the current navigation accuracy, mitigating immediate risk during the Kuiper Belt transits. However, perpetually running the legacy code means foregoing significant gains in power efficiency and data throughput promised by 2.0. A compromise could involve tuning the 2.0 patch to maintain a restricted subset of the most critical heuristic functions for essential deep-space maneuverability.",
